  "title": "A Sharp Width-Ten Gap for Defective Valid-Extension Sets of Finite Gilbreath Sequences",
  "batch_label": "84",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For every n >= 3 and every normalized strictly increasing Gilbreath sequence S in G_n, if its full two-sided valid-extension set K_S is not the candidate parity interval C_S, then |K_S| >= 10. The bound is sharp, attained by S=(2,3,5,9,15). Consequently |K_S| <= 9 holds exactly when K_S=C_S and A(S)<=7; this reduces the still-unresolved original classification to the four small ordered anti-diagonal types stated in evidence/threshold_lemma.md, without claiming an explicit classification of all top rows realizing those types.",
